# PROBER_DAEMON_MODE=on is the boot-contract opt-in this scenario requires. A
# USR2 binary upgrade cannot be delivered to a foregrounded (daemon off) master
# -- ngx_signal_handler drops NGX_CHANGEBIN when getppid()==ngx_parent, which
# always holds for a daemon-off master whose parent is prober_boot's `&`
# launcher, so the master logs "the changing binary signal is ignored" and no
# new master forks. The opt-in inverts prober_check_conf's daemon gate (it now
# demands `daemon on;` plus a pidfile at $PROBER_PREFIX/nginx.pid) and switches
# prober_boot/prober_stop from tracking the master by $! to tracking it by that
# pidfile. See usr2-state-machine and backend-usr2-keepalive's env for the same
# contract.
#
# Sourced per-scenario in a run-scenario.sh subprocess, so the opt-in cannot
# leak into any other scenario's boot.
PROBER_DAEMON_MODE=on
